      texto: 'If you charge clients automatically, federal and state law expect clear disclosure and express consent. The Restore Online Shoppers Confidence Act, 15 U.S.C. § 8403, requires that material terms of a negative option arrangement sold online be clearly disclosed and that the consumer give express informed consent before being charged, with a simple way to stop recurring charges. Several states add their own automatic renewal statutes. An electronically signed agreement that states these terms is valid under the ESIGN Act, 15 U.S.C. § 7001.',
